      "limitations": [
        "the fixed runtime state covers the x86-64 integer core and preserves unmodeled logical state outside generated code",
        "lowering schema 9 accepts only canonical encodings without legacy prefixes or semantically redundant REX extension bits: REX.W full-width x86-64 GPR MOV, ADD/SUB, and AND/OR/XOR forms with supported register/immediate LowIR shapes; full-width register-only CMP 39/3B and register/immediate CMP 81/7, 83/7, and 3D; full-width register-only TEST 85 and register/immediate TEST F7/0 and A9; arithmetic and CMP forms retain their scalar flag computations without CMP writing either operand, while logical and TEST forms compute architecture-defined flags and preserve AF in the NeverD state model without TEST writing either operand; canonical C3 RET or C2 iw RET imm16 terminates a return block, canonical EB cb or E9 cd terminates a direct-branch block, and canonical legacy-prefix-free traditional Jcc comprises JO/JNO short 70/71 cb or near 0F 80/81 cd, JB/JAE 72/73 cb or 0F 82/83 cd, JE/JNE 74/75 cb or 0F 84/85 cd, JBE/JA 76/77 cb or 0F 86/87 cd, JS/JNS 78/79 cb or 0F 88/89 cd, JP/JNP 7A/7B cb or 0F 8A/8B cd, JL/JGE 7C/7D cb or 0F 8C/8D cd, and JLE/JG 7E/7F cb or 0F 8E/8F cd; reserved F7 /1 and every other encoding fail closed",
        "JRCXZ/JECXZ/JCXZ and LOOP/LOOPE/LOOPNE remain unpublished and are rejected before object emission",
        "ordinary guest-memory operations, partial-register forms, any instruction outside the exact published subset, all other control flow, and unimplemented LowIR operations are rejected before object emission",
        "the C, Python, and CLI object requests emit only audited little-endian AArch64 ELF or Mach-O relocatable objects; those three surfaces do not link, load, publish, dispatch, execute, or debug code",
        "proof-gated semantic simplification and LLVM's default O2 optimization pipeline are composed before audited object emission",
        "a non-zero generated-object byte budget is measured after indivisible LLVM emission into a private buffer; an oversized object is rejected before publication and artifact audit, while typed telemetry may report its exact observed size above the requested limit",
        "the Python surface raises TranslationError with TranslationErrorCode for native translation failures, while local argument validation raises TypeError or ValueError",
        "the standalone pre-allocation JITLink graph audit does not itself link, allocate, resolve, load, publish, dispatch, or execute code",
        "native linking and execution are a separate experimental C++ boundary and do not turn the C, Python, or CLI object APIs into execution interfaces"
      ],
